  At unskilled or basic cone of cold does [(XL/2) + 1 ]d6 damage per
hit.  It's in the form of a ray.  A monster hit with XL:30 basic- cone
of cold takes 16d6 damage = average 56.

  At Skilled or Expert cone of cold hits a 3x3 square of spaces 2-9
times, but only does [(XL/2) + 1] damage per hit per square.  So 9 * 5 =
45 hits.  At XL:30 damage is 16.  (18 if Int is greater than 18.)
45 * 16 = 720.  820 if Int is greater than 18.  That's total damage.

  For an individual monster it's average 5 hits times 16 damage = 80
points of damage for an single monster.  That's still quite a bit better
than at basic-.  (Not to mention the capital improvements to the area by
freezing water and lava.)

  That's still major amounts of damage, but in the range of an artillery
stonk, not a tactical nuclear missile.

  That's probably not a significant different, BION.  80 points of
damage will probably take out most monsters.  Two casts on the same
point should clear the area.  Anything more just adds to the overkill.
(That explains why skilled+ cone of cold didn't seem underpowered when I
cast it, or when watching someone else cast it.)

